sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor HW as Health worker
  participant App as PWA (SyncQueue + IndexedDB)
  participant API as FastAPI
  participant ML as ScreeningPipeline + ModelRegistry
  participant DB as Database
  actor SP as Specialist

  HW->>App: Choose patient and eye, take photo
  alt online
    App->>API: POST /api/screenings (image, patient_id, eye, client_uuid, captured_at)
  else offline
    App->>App: Save to IndexedDB queue (status pending)
    Note over App,API: When the connection returns, retry with exponential backoff and jitter
    App->>API: POST /api/screenings (same client_uuid, X-Sync-Attempt n)
  end
  API->>DB: client_uuid already stored?
  alt duplicate (reply was lost earlier)
    API-->>App: 200 original record (duplicate = true)
  else new
    API->>ML: validate type/size, quality gate, fundus check
    alt unusable image
      ML-->>API: blocking issue (blank, too small, not a fundus photo)
      API-->>App: 422 plain-language reason, nothing saved
    else usable
      ML->>ML: score with every registered model, then RiskPolicy gives band, action, refer_suggested
      ML-->>API: one outcome per condition (unavailable models flagged)
      API->>DB: screening + diagnosis_results + sync_log + audit (no referral yet)
      API-->>App: 201 result + ReferralAdvisor recommendation
    end
  end
  App-->>HW: Result cards and recommendation (no referral needed / refer recommended / uncertain)
  opt health worker decides to ask
    HW->>API: POST /api/screenings/{id}/ask-specialist (question)
    API->>DB: referral (reason, question, review target) + audit
    API-->>HW: Awaiting specialist
  end

  SP->>API: GET /api/reviews/queue
  API-->>SP: Cases health workers sent, with their question, overdue first
  SP->>API: POST /api/reviews/{id} (approve | override + reason | request_retake | comment)
  API->>DB: INSERT review_event (never UPDATE or DELETE), close referral
  App->>API: GET /api/sync/pull?since=last_pull
  API-->>App: Decisions on this worker's screenings
  App-->>HW: Status updated (reviewed / retake requested)
